---
import { brand } from "@tandoor/brand";
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${brand.name}`}
  description="How Tandoor processes Telegram messages, connected Google account data, and workspace information."
  currentPage="privacy"
>
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="prose-page brand-prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: November 14, 2026</p>

    <p>
      Tandoor is a private Telegram agent available to invited users. This
      policy explains what information Tandoor processes when people chat
      with the agent or connect a Google account.
    </p>

    <h2>Information Tandoor Processes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Telegram messages, attachments, account identifiers, and basic profile information needed to provide the service.</li>
      <li>Prompts, agent responses, tool activity, and files saved in a Tandoor workspace.</li>
      <li>When you connect Google, your account email and the Google data accessed or changed while carrying out your requests. This may include Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Docs, Sheets, Classroom, Contacts, and other services listed on Google's consent screen.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How Google Data Is Used</h2>
    <p>
      Tandoor uses Google data to carry out the actions you ask the agent to
      perform, such as finding information, preparing summaries, or making
      requested changes. When users configure recurring tasks, Tandoor may
      access Google data at the scheduled time, for example to check email
      or prepare a daily brief. This is task-specific access, not continuous
      synchronization. Tandoor does not sell Google data, use it for
      advertising, or use it to train general AI models.
    </p>
    <p>
      Information needed to answer a request may be included in the agent's
      conversation and sent to the AI model provider configured for that
      worker. The provider processes that information to generate the
      response under its own terms and privacy practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Storage and Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Tandoor stores conversation history, workspace files, and relevant
      agent results on the server where Tandoor runs. Google account
      credentials are stored in Gog's encrypted file keyring within the
      corresponding worker's persistent storage. Data remains there until
      it is removed by the service operator or the underlying storage is
      deleted. Revoking Google access stops future access but does not
      automatically remove information already present in conversation
      history or files.
    </p>

    <h2>Personal and Group Spaces</h2>
    <p>
      Personal Google credentials are kept in the user's personal worker.
      Group topics share the group's conversation and workspace. If you ask
      Tandoor to use your personal Google account from a group, the result
      may be included in that group's conversation and visible to its
      members. A Google account connected as a shared group account is
      available to the group worker.
    </p>
    <p>
      The agent running in a worker can access that worker's files and
      connected credentials to complete requests. Personal workers and
      group workers have separate persistent storage, except that members
      of a group intentionally share that group's worker and workspace.
    </p>

    <h2>Service Providers</h2>
    <p>
      Tandoor relies on Telegram to deliver messages, Google to provide
      connected services, and the configured AI model provider to generate
      responses. These providers process information as needed to provide
      their services and under their own policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Your Choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can revoke Tandoor's Google access from your Google Account
      security settings. To ask about removing data stored by Tandoor,
      contact the operator at{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${brand.contactEmail}`}>{brand.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions or data removal requests, email{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${brand.contactEmail}`}>{brand.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
